1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the flying thing
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,920
kick a pebble and it goes flying off.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
To the type who was always goofing off,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:38,680
Even if I lose my spirit somewhere,
all that's piled up is gas.

6
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:43,880
With one yawn,
the unchanging streets feel even gentler.

7
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,720
The crows are cawing,
so the sun has already set.

8
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,900
Do you really want some yakitori?

9
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:11,080
Thank you for watching.

10
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:27,400
Welcome, Dachio-san.

11
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,520
Ryotsu

12
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,140
Hey, Ryotsu!

13
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:43,400
Ōhana-kun, what is this tea?

14
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,920
It's been reheated and left like this.

15
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,220
Ryotsu

16
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,740
Hurry up, Ōhana-kun!

17
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,120
Go!

18
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,340
Ow ow!

19
00:01:53,900 --> 00:02:19,760
Who the fuck is this bastard!

20
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:21,340
The world's at peace, right?

21
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:24,300
Look, the streets are
overflowing with smiles,

22
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:26,140
with no big incidents happening.

23
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:28,020
It's just the same old town, isn't it?

24
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:33,800
See? Even the ostriches
are running around happily.

25
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,580
W-what?

26
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:37,980
Ostrich!

27
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:41,220
Thief! Thief!

28
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,540
Hey, give back the Saikon!

29
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:01,760
Such nice weather, isn't it?

30
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:04,100
It is.

31
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,220
Did something just pass by?

32
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,280
Yeah.

33
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:16,480
Why is there an ostrich in town?

34
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,780
It's bound to crash if it
doesn't obey the traffic lights.

35
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,700
Our place was wrecked by Taki!

36
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,580
Anyway, catch it quickly!

37
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:24,580
Excuse me.

38
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:27,360
I've just ordered all officers to deploy,

39
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,660
so it will be captured shortly.

40
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:30,360
Please wait a little while longer.

41
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:32,920
So then,

42
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:36,640
the order is to capture the
ostrich immediately upon sighting it.

43
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,000
All units, deploy!

44
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:38,760
Roger!

45
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:43,820
There it is! Chase it!

46
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,080
Wait, wait!

47
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,480
Hold it right there!

48
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,580
Damn, what a speed!

49
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:57,920
Yeah, ostriches can apparently run up to 70 km/h.
Say that first!

50
00:03:58,640 --> 00:04:04,120
But why is it even here?
Ostriches are African animals, right?

51
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:13,560
That's right. No zoo or breeding farm has reported an escaped ostrich,
and I've never heard of wild ostriches in Japan.

52
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,360
What now, Ryotsu?

53
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,120
Just in time!

54
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,220
Chase that thing!

55
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:21,960
Catch up to what?

56
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:23,380
Just go!

57
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:24,920
I don't get it, but...

58
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,620
Let's go, boss.

59
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,100
Alright!

60
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:35,320
What?

61
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:36,540
Look!

62
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:42,140
Found it!

63
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:43,220
Okay, here we go!

64
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:55,700
Yay!

65
00:04:56,180 --> 00:04:57,600
Can't even reach seventy
kilometers an hour, can it?

66
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,520
What?!

67
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,140
You bastard!

68
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:17,740
Whoa! What do you mean,
"idiot"? Calling me an idiot!

69
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:21,800
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
"If you're so mad, try catching me," it says!

70
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,980
We don't need to be told that!

71
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,520
Scary, scary, scary!

72
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,920
It says it's a pointless effort!

73
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:30,300
Cocky for a mere ostrich!

74
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:34,700
Wait, you understand ostrich language?

75
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:36,680
Now that you mention it...

76
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:40,220
But I kind of feel like
that's what it's saying.

77
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,500
Waaah!

78
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:43,140
Hey! Stop right there!

79
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,760
Milord!

80
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,480
You cheated on me again, didn't you!

81
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:52,800
You're one to talk! You were
walking arm in arm with another man!

82
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,700
Wait!

83
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:01,580
Wait! Sesso!

84
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:08,460
Damn that bastard! Where the hell did it go?

85
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:17,320
Wait, that bastard... is it male? It said
"ore," so you can tell that much?

86
00:06:17,970 --> 00:06:22,440
Yeah, well, that's the thing...

87
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,860
Sensei, senpai, yan kokokoko haa!

88
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:26,680
It's close!

89
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:30,160
Look, wait! Catch that ostrich from before!

90
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:30,780
Whoa!

91
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:33,660
Get out with Sā-ro-san!
Let's call the police!

92
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:35,720
That's why I'm the police!

93
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:36,600
Whoa!

94
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,560
Damn it, it got away!

95
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:43,860
Let's head back and figure out a plan.

96
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:44,480
Get out!

97
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:53,100
What? You understand ostrich language?

98
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:56,020
Well, sort of, I guess.

99
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:59,300
Still, that's amazing.
Just like you, Ryo-san.

100
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:03,000
Well, Ryo-chan is practically a wild animal himself,
after all.

101
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,300
True enough.

102
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:05,460
What did you say?

103
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:09,700
Chief, what's going on?

104
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:10,420
Alright.

105
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:17,700
What is the meaning of this?

106
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:19,880
Can't you see for yourself?

107
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:25,280
You've been appointed head of the Katsushika
district ostrich countermeasures headquarters.

108
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:29,620
But why me?

109
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:32,560
Well, I heard you can
understand ostrich language.

110
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:35,880
I thought no one but you could
handle this important role.

111
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,140
I'm counting on you.

112
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:44,320
Surely you're not trying
to pass this off on me

113
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:46,860
just because catching the
ostrich is such a hassle?

114
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,040
Bingo!

115
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,498
Anyway,

116
00:07:52,548 --> 00:07:56,391
from now on, you take responsibility
and do your best to catch that ostrich,

117
00:07:56,441 --> 00:07:57,340
got it?!

118
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:58,700
Yes, yes.

119
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:02,760
Damn it,
all of you are dumping your trouble on me!

120
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:05,840
And why am I included in this...?

121
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,720
I can't stand being
made a fool of like this!

122
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:15,840
So do we have some kind of plan?

123
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:20,740
No! Besides,
I don't even know how to catch an ostrich.

124
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:21,365
Hah.

125
00:08:21,415 --> 00:08:25,920
At this rate,
when will I ever get back to Shiraume duty?

126
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,440
Oh!

127
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,640
W-what happened?

128
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,360
I've got it!

129
00:08:39,780 --> 00:08:42,340
Senpai, what is this?

130
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:47,220
We'll dazzle the bastard with these
outfits and grab him while he's distracted.

131
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:49,480
Can I write the kanji chart?

132
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:52,940
Th-th-the big one!

133
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:56,760
Calm down,
we're sexy female ostriches right now.

134
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,220
Female ostriches.

135
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:06,660
Handsome man, come here, darling.

136
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:14,420
Ooh! C-c-c-cluck!

137
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:17,540
C-c-c-cluck!

138
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:20,240
It's working!
Alright, Honda, don't let it escape!

139
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:21,180
Roger!

140
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:23,600
C-c-c-cluck!

141
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:24,740
Yaah!

142
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,620
C-c-c-cluck!

143
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,940
Hey! S-s-stop right there!

144
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,000
Uhahaha!

145
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:31,900
Co, co, co, co, coo!

146
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:34,500
Senpai, why are you running away?!

147
00:09:34,800 --> 00:09:37,340
Nakagawa, you bastard!
I'm getting proposed to!

148
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,160
He wants me to lay his eggs!

149
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,420
As if I could lay eggs!

150
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:45,100
Think Ryotsu's about to get caught soon?

151
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:46,580
I hope so.

152
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:50,080
R-Ryotsu!

153
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:51,400
That outfit!

154
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:56,380
Ryotsu!

155
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:57,020
Chief!

156
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:13,580
Cluck!

157
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:16,100
Cluck! Cluck-cluck-cluck!

158
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:19,520
A happy home with the two of us?!

159
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:20,840
Cluck-cluck! Cluck!

160
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:24,320
What? You want us to have enough
kids to make a soccer team?

161
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,360
That's impossible, obviously!

162
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,220
Hey! Stay away!

163
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:30,600
Whoa!

164
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:31,640
Ugh... nngh...

165
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,680
Whoa!

166
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:38,900
Whoaaa!

167
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:56,160
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

168
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,320
Are you all right?

169
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:00,580
Thank goodness the Honda's safe!

170
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:04,860
I see.

171
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:08,260
So that's how it was.

172
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,340
What's it saying?

173
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:14,740
Apparently,
this one lived around Kameari Park.

174
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:18,340
Since the place it hatched
from was Kameari Park,

175
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:20,300
it's said it stayed there the whole time.

176
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,620
Why would an ostrich egg
be in a place like that?

177
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,120
As for that much...

178
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,420
Did someone drop it while carrying it?

179
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:31,700
Or did someone abandon it?

180
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:33,420
Poor thing.

181
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:36,560
All alone, in a city like this.

182
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,760
What a tearjerker of a story.

183
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:44,220
What, not just one bird?!

184
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:08,140
Why are there so many of them?

185
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,620
With them breeding over and over,

186
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:13,700
they've somehow turned into a huge family.

187
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:15,220
What are we going to do?

188
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:16,880
If there are that many of them,

189
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:19,500
even a zoo won't take them in.

190
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:22,540
Leave it to you, Countermeasures Chief.

191
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:26,160
I did catch the ostrich, didn't I?

192
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,700
So the other ostriches don't
cause trouble for the town,

193
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:33,540
come up with a proper plan.

194
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:34,880
This is ridiculous!

195
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:36,400
Whoa!

196
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,140
Whoa!

197
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:38,840
W-what did you say?

198
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,620
Don't go making things up!

199
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,020
What's it saying?

200
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,040
It says I'm its life savior or something.

201
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,840
And that it hopes we'll
get along in the future.

202
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:47,940
Whoa!

203
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:48,200
Whoa!

204
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:51,400
Well, looks like everyone
really took a liking to Ryo-chan.

205
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:53,020
Good, good.

206
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:56,020
Then I'm counting on you,
countermeasures HQ chief.

207
00:12:57,020 --> 00:12:57,860
No way!

208
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:24,180
Yo! Everybody awake?

209
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:31,080
Alright, let's give it our best again today.

210
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:34,736
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

211
00:13:34,786 --> 00:13:38,492
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

212
00:13:38,542 --> 00:13:42,223
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

213
00:13:42,273 --> 00:13:46,004
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

214
00:13:46,054 --> 00:13:49,723
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

215
00:13:49,773 --> 00:13:53,491
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

216
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:57,235
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

217
00:13:57,285 --> 00:14:00,940
Cluck, cluck, cluck,
cluck, cluck, cluck, cluck.

218
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:05,260
Now, I'll announce today's assignments.

219
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,800
Dachō no Suke and Dachōemon.

220
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,020
Dachomi and Takohaibi.

221
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:12,920
Dachōjirō, Dachobe, Dachoko, and Dachogoro,
head to the shopping district.

222
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:14,920
You, come with me.

223
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:18,200
The rest of you, clean the park.

224
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:24,000
As a special favor,
you're allowed to stay here.

225
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,400
But you have to earn
your own living expenses.

226
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,320
Our motto is simple.

227
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:32,760
Those who don't work don't eat! Understood?

228
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:33,640
Whoa!

229
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:36,180
All right, get to work!

230
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:38,900
Watch out for cars!

231
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,140
G-good morning!

232
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:52,760
Now then, from this point on, the ostrich

233
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,360
Special Patrol Squad, moving out!

234
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:57,220
Yeah, I'm counting on you!

235
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:58,880
Alright! Go!

236
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:03,280
Deliver this right away!

237
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:05,320
I'm counting on you.

238
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,920
Geez, why is it so crowded already?

239
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,500
We're not gonna make it at this rate!

240
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:27,260
You're at it too

241
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:34,860
Mommy, where are you?

242
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:39,060
What's wrong,
did you get separated from your mom?

243
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:42,660
Right, leave it to us.

244
00:15:43,460 --> 00:15:44,020
Please.

245
00:15:45,980 --> 00:15:50,640
Excuse me.

246
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:54,100
Is there anyone here
who's this girl's mother?

247
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:55,920
Mom.

248
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:56,640
Mommy.

249
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:58,720
Mom.

250
00:15:58,720 --> 00:15:59,720
Mommy.

251
00:16:00,420 --> 00:16:01,420
Yuki-chan.

252
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:02,560
Mommy.

253
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:03,940
Mommy.

254
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:05,020
Yuki-chan.

255
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:06,400
Thank you.

256
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:07,720
Thank you very much.

257
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:09,620
Yes?

258
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:12,400
I just did what any ostrich would do.

259
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,000
Hey.

260
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,020
Thief!

261
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:18,220
Let's go!

262
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:22,020
We did it!

263
00:16:22,020 --> 00:16:23,640
Hey, you on the motorbike!

264
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:25,420
Hold it right there!

265
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:30,720
Don't underestimate an ostrich's speed!

266
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,360
Don't just stop quietly!

267
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,500
No way! I'm not getting caught!

268
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:41,080
There! Loaded up like this,
you can't get through, can you?

269
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:43,860
No way I'm letting it escape!
Ostrich squad, move out!

270
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:51,640
Serves you right!

271
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:55,820
Damn it! We couldn't get out?

272
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:00,200
Send them in!

273
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:03,640
What the heck is this?!

274
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:14,760
You're under arrest for
snatching a bag in the act!

275
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:19,340
Wow, you really did great!

276
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:24,500
The ostriches' teamwork is flawless!
They're the talk of Kameari now!

277
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:25,960
That's amazing!

278
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:30,360
That's right, that's right.
Now go on and praise us even more.

279
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:33,200
They really are amazing, those ostriches.

280
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:33,760
What?

281
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:37,300
Working so hard and united
like this in a city like this...

282
00:17:37,300 --> 00:17:38,620
I really admire them.

283
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:41,120
Hey, hey,
don't just keep praising the ostriches!

284
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:43,780
I'm the one who trained those guys,
you know!

285
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:47,360
But nothing about you
is written there, Senpai.

286
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,300
What do you mean?!

287
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:52,820
For them,
who live sturdily without anyone's help,

288
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:56,640
the Katsushika Police Station is going to
present a letter of commendation and a cash award.

289
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:59,880
What? I haven't heard a thing about this!

290
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:03,560
Your work this time was truly splendid.

291
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:06,780
Please keep working hard
for the people of the town.

292
00:18:06,780 --> 00:18:09,080
I'm counting on you,
all of you in the Ostrich Unit.

293
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:10,660
Hold on a second!

294
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:16,120
Chief, why do only the
ostriches get commended?

295
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:18,400
What about my share? My share...

296
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:20,660
What are you talking about?

297
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,620
It was the ostriches who did the work,
not you.

298
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:27,180
Big deal!
I'm the Chief, and Colonel Ostrich is too...

299
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:31,500
Aren't I basically their supervisor,
the one who trains them?

300
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:36,080
Idiot! If you're a supervisor, shouldn't you
be happy when your subordinates are commended?

301
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:39,640
Just because you weren't praised,
you're flustered and panicking.

302
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,080
What a disgrace.

303
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:43,340
Look at the ostriches.

304
00:18:44,020 --> 00:18:49,060
All for one, one for all. This commendation
is for everyone's hard work, isn't it?

305
00:18:50,660 --> 00:18:57,740
Don't you think so? Eza, that's not what I mean.
There's also a plan to build a new gymnasium soon. Please continue...

306
00:18:57,740 --> 00:18:58,580
I'm counting on you.

307
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:03,340
That's tough.
I'll be watching to see how this turns out.

308
00:19:04,460 --> 00:19:04,920
Me

309
00:19:10,340 --> 00:19:12,940
Mm. Well, thanks for all your hard work.

310
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:19,040
Yes, thank you very much.
Doesn't this feel a little light?

311
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:23,100
Hey, what's going on with this?

312
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:25,560
You didn't eat it, did you?

313
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:42,220
Peeping, peeping!

314
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:53,780
What on earth is going on here?

315
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:56,120
I thought they were helping
people during the day,

316
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:58,440
but they're up to this in
the middle of the night!

317
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:04,120
So ostriches really are
just wild animals after all.

318
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:06,320
Don't you ever come back!

319
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:12,480
The Ostrich Corps is a total failure!

320
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:15,680
So they really were wild animals after all.

321
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:18,240
They ate delivered pizza,

322
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:21,200
and raiding garbage dumps is definitely going too far,
isn't it?

323
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:24,440
You were such a popular
star at the zoo, though.

324
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:27,380
Booms really are fleeting, aren't they?

325
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:29,800
Serves you right!

326
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:32,860
It's because they outwitted
me and stole the credit.

327
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:25,800
Those ostriches,
did they learn their lesson?

328
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:28,620
That should keep them
from going out for a while.

329
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,860
Serves them right for getting cocky.

330
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:39,760
W-what?

331
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:41,460
Something's off here.

332
00:21:41,460 --> 00:21:42,880
What happened?

333
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:45,680
W-what is it?

334
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:47,080
Whoa, what's this?

335
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:50,100
The ostriches are innocent,
the culprit is this guy!

336
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:53,100
H-how did this get here?!

337
00:21:53,800 --> 00:21:54,280
Whoa!

338
00:21:55,340 --> 00:21:56,660
Idiot, idiot, idiot, idiot!

339
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:04,620
Uh-oh, this is really bad.

340
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:08,140
Let's hide somewhere
before the Chief finds out.

341
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:10,260
Too late.

342
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:19,220
Don't you feel sorry for the ostriches?

343
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:22,780
There's a lot of circumstances behind this.

344
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:27,990
Yes. Actually,
to cover for the ostriches' mistake,

345
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:30,600
I took their place.

346
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:32,440
That's what he says, anyway.

347
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,500
He says it's just as he said.

348
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:41,400
Hmph.

349
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:44,240
Ow Stop it!

350
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:45,420
Please, stop!

351
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:48,740
Don't give me made-up translations,
you idiot!

352
00:22:48,740 --> 00:22:52,360
General, don't hold back,
give them a thorough lesson!

353
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:53,700
Please, stop!

354
00:22:53,700 --> 00:22:57,420
I was just giving you the diagnosis,
so stop!

355
00:22:58,200 --> 00:22:59,420
Please, stop!

356
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:09,498
Coming, Dachonosuke-san,

357
00:23:09,548 --> 00:23:11,800
Dachoko-san, sorry for the wait.

358
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:15,292
Right, right. Dacholina-sama,

359
00:23:15,342 --> 00:23:17,680
you want water, right?
I'll bring it right away.

360
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,970
Dachosaburo-sama, your back hurts.

361
00:23:22,020 --> 00:23:24,160
I'll give you a massage later.

362
00:23:28,660 --> 00:23:30,880
Everyone, have a good day!

363
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:34,200
Please do your best again today!

364
00:23:37,100 --> 00:23:40,240
Hey, why am I being treated
like I'm beneath an ostrich?!

365
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:42,040
I can't accept this!

366
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:52,840
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

367
00:23:54,020 --> 00:23:56,900
I walked while looking back

368
00:23:56,900 --> 00:23:59,520
Led by the hand of Gacha

369
00:24:00,540 --> 00:24:02,700
The feeling I had back then

370
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:06,740
A strange feeling

371
00:24:07,380 --> 00:24:08,200
So

372
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:11,940
On the tiles of the arcade street

373
00:24:11,940 --> 00:24:14,040
Only the black ones

374
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:17,720
I tried walking on them

375
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:25,840
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten

376
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:30,000
Politicians with their
self-important faces won't do

377
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:33,340
Nor the aunties with blue eyeshadow

378
00:24:33,820 --> 00:24:38,900
Go on, turn that corner

379
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:44,100
You'll get to see everyone, everyone

380
00:24:45,900 --> 00:24:48,740
Over there is Kameari,

381
00:24:49,580 --> 00:24:52,040
surely Kameari,

382
00:24:53,300 --> 00:24:57,300
everyone, come to our town!

383
00:24:57,300 --> 00:25:01,960
Over there is Kameari,

384
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:05,200
surely Kameari,

385
00:25:06,020 --> 00:25:10,420
everyone, come to our town!

386
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:12,040
Thank you.

387
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:18,260
I started training in shogi because
I really wanted to beat the Chief,

388
00:25:18,260 --> 00:25:20,580
but I ended up playing some crazy shogi.

389
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:23,240
Alright,
now I'll fight with my life on the line!

390
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:26,860
Vacuum tornado! Dragon god's dance!

391
00:25:26,860 --> 00:25:28,400
Wait, this is shogi, right?

392
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:31,980
Next time, a brutal shogi battle,
see you then!

393
00:25:44,300 --> 00:25:45,700
Thanks.

